10
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:11,000
The Last House on the Left is a 2009 rape and revenge film directed by
Dennis Iliadis and written by Adam Alleca and Carl Ellsworth.

11
00:51:47,500 --> 00:51:53,500
A remake of the 1972 film of the same name, it stars Tony Goldwyn, Monica Potter, Garret Dillahunt,
Aaron Paul, Spencer Treat Clark, Riki Lindhome, Martha MacIsaac, and Sara Paxton.

12
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
The film follows Mari Collingwood, a teenager who is abducted, raped,
and left for dead by a family of violent fugitives.

13
01:01:12,500 --> 01:01:18,500
When her parents learn what was done to her, they seek vengeance against the family,
who have taken shelter at their summer home during a thunderstorm.

14
01:05:55,000 --> 01:06:01,000
The rights to The Last House on the Left were picked up by Rogue Pictures in 2006, with the remake
being the first film produced by Craven's newly formed studio Midnight Pictures.

15
01:10:37,500 --> 01:10:43,500
Craven, who wrote and directed the original film, was interested to see what kind of film could be made on a larger
budget, as the limited funds forced him to remove scenes he had wanted to film to tell a complete story.

16
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:26,000
One of the elements Iliadis wanted to avoid with the film, given its
graphic nature, was turning it into "torture porn".

17
01:20:02,500 --> 01:20:08,500
For Craven and Iliadis, the film primarily illustrates how even the most normal
of families can be driven to commit evil acts if pushed too far.

18
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:51,000
The original script by Alleca included elements of supernatural horror, which
prompted the studio to reject it and bring in Ellsworth for rewrites.

19
01:29:27,500 --> 01:29:33,500
Principal photography began in March 2008 in Cape Town and
Helderberg Nature Reserve and concluded in May.

20
01:34:10,000 --> 01:34:16,000
The Last House on the Left was theatrically released in the United States on March 13, 2009, and was
a modest box office success, grossing $46 million against its $15 million budget.

21
01:38:52,500 --> 01:38:58,500
The film received mixed reviews from critics, with several deeming it worthy of praise in comparison to
other horror films and remakes in general, while others considered it inferior to the original.

22
01:43:35,000 --> 01:43:41,000
The film explores themes of lake, rape, kidnapping, psychopath, sadistic.

23
01:48:17,500 --> 01:48:23,500
The tone is lighthearted and dark and emotional.
